    "title": "One person dead following motorcycle crash in Georgia - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ohio Statewide Staff ,\n2 hours ago GEORGIA — One person is dead following a motorcycle crash in Taylor County on Wednesday evening, according to the Taylor County Sheriff’s Office.\nAuthorities said the crash occurred sometime before 6 p.m. on Newsome Road. The sheriff’s office reported that the motorcyclist lost control of the bike, left the roadway, and struck a drain pipe and a tree.\nThe driver was pronounced dead at the scene.\nOfficials have not yet released the identity of the victim as they work to notify family members.\nThe Georgia State Patrol is investigating the crash.\nAnyone with additional information is asked to contact the Taylor County Sheriff’s Office at 478-862-5444.\nThe post One person dead following motorcycle crash in Georgia first appeared on Ohio Statewide .\n9",
    "summary": "By Ohio Statewide Staff , 1 hours ago GEORGIA — One person is dead following a motorcycle crash in Taylor County on Wednesday evening, according to the Taylor County Sheriff’s Office. The sheriff’s office reported that the motorcyclist lost control of the bike, left the roadway, and struck a drain pipe and a tree. Officials have not yet released the identity of the victim as they work to notify family members. Anyone with additional information is asked to contact the Taylor County Sheriff’s Office at 478-862-5444.",
